leonardo (0.1.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix CreateBucket and PutObject failing with fsync_on_write enabled
    (ClosedChannelException after Jackson closed the stream).
  * Hide keys whose latest version is a delete marker from ListObjects;
    emit VersionId "null" for unversioned objects so clients can empty
    buckets.
  * DeleteObjects honours the per-entry VersionId instead of stacking
    delete markers; DELETE ?versionId= echoes x-amz-version-id and
    x-amz-delete-marker.
  * Suspended versioning keeps the real versions and holds a single null
    version; overwrites no longer leak the previous payload file.
  * CopyObject: ?versionId= sources, x-amz-metadata-directive and
    x-amz-tagging-directive REPLACE, self-copy requires REPLACE.
  * UploadPartCopy honours x-amz-copy-source-range; CompleteMultipartUpload
    validates parts (InvalidPart, EntityTooSmall) before touching the upload.
  * Keys with a trailing slash, response-* header overrides, XML bodies on
    412 and 416, NoSuchTagSet on untagged buckets.
  * Authentication failures report InvalidAccessKeyId and
    SignatureDoesNotMatch; SigV2 presigned URLs are accepted.
  * Add tools/smoke-test.py and tools/smoke-test-mc.sh.

 -- Lucas Holt <luke@foolishgames.com>  Sun, 01 Nov 2026 05:00:00 +0000

leonardo (0.1.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix botocore compatibility: HeadObject without Accept header, SigV4
    for percent-encoded keys, POST bodies without Content-Type.
  * CompleteMultipartUpload honours bucket versioning, immutability and
    retention and returns x-amz-version-id.
  * Keep delete markers in version history; store x-amz-tagging and
    Cache-Control, Content-Disposition, Content-Encoding,
    Content-Language and Expires.
  * Validate multipart upload and object IDs before they reach the
    filesystem (path injection).
  * Keep-alive fixes: drain unread request bodies, never send 100 Continue
    for a rejected PutObject or UploadPart.
  * Bump AssertJ to 3.27.7 (GHSA-rqfh-9r24-8c9r).
  * Add tools/minio-to-leonardo.py migration script.

 -- Lucas Holt <luke@foolishgames.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

